       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">POSITIVE</span> · The Better India · 2026-10-15 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>73-Year-Old Retired Banker Wins Four National Powerlifting Golds</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#positive</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>D V Shankar Rao, a 73-year-old retired State Bank of India employee, has become a national powerlifting champion. After undergoing coronary artery bypass surgery in 2012, Rao began focusing on fitness in February 2025 to improve his health following a long career.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-15/73-year-old-retired-banker-wins-four-national-powerlifting-g.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Within six months of training at a local gym in Bhadrachalam, Telangana, Rao entered competitive powerlifting. In August 2025, he won gold medals in squat, bench press, and deadlift at a national event in Kozhikode, securing the overall National Masters Classic title. His family now supports his athletic journey, which he describes as a medical miracle.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately captures the subject's background, surgery, and national powerlifting achievements.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
