     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-15 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>90,000 Devotees Celebrate Fifth Day of Dasara in Vijayawada</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Approximately 90,000 devotees visited the Sri Durga Malleswara Swamyvarla Devasthanam on Indrakeeladri Thursday to witness Goddess Kanaka Durga adorned as Sri Lalitha Tripura Sundari Devi. The temple hosted special rituals and multiple haratis during the auspicious pradosha period as part of the nine-day Dasara festivities.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-15/90000-devotees-celebrate-fifth-day-of-dasara-in-vijayawada.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The celebrations included a traditional Nagarotsavam procession along the Krishna riverfront and ghat road. Accompanied by Vedic chants, traditional music, and dance performances, the event drew thousands of spectators. Devotees believe observing the deities during this procession brings prosperity, peace, and the fulfillment of wishes.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is highly dense and accurately summarizes the event, the specific deity alankaram, the procession details, and the attendance figures provided in the source text.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/cities/Vijayawada/90000-devotees-throng-vijayawada-kanaka-durga-temple-on-fifth-day-of-dasara-celebrations/article71588749.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       <div class="cityguide"><b>City guide</b><p>More on <a href="https://bharatdn.com/city/vijayawada/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Vijayawada</a> - census 2011 population, live weather and air quality, local food and getaways.</p></div>
