     <article class="story single" data-beat="finance">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">FINANCE</span> · BS Personal Finance · 2026-10-15 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Bonfiglioli Transmissions IPO Opens for Bidding at ₹558–₹586 Price Band</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#finance</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Bonfiglioli Transmissions, India's largest power transmission and industrial drive solutions provider, opened its ₹2,533.66 crore IPO for bidding on October 15. The offer is entirely an offer for sale by promoters with a price band of ₹558 to ₹586 per share. The issue closes on October 19.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-15/bonfiglioli-transmissions-ipo-opens-for-bidding-at-558586-pr.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Analysts are largely bullish on the company, citing a strong dealer network and a diversified business model. SBI Securities recommends subscribing to the issue, while Anand Rathi has assigned a 'Subscribe for Long Term' rating. The company serves the Industry &amp; Automation, Off-Highway Mobility, and Wind energy verticals.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately summarizes the IPO details, pricing, and analyst sentiment provided in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.business-standard.com/markets/news/bonfiglioli-transmissions-ipo-experts-recommend-subscribe-gmp-signals-30-listing-gain-126101500255_1.html" rel="noopener">BS Personal Finance</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
