       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENTERTAINMENT</span> · Variety · 2026-10-15 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Carlo Rambaldi Honored with Posthumous Hollywood Walk of Fame Star</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#entertainment</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Special effects master Carlo Rambaldi is being honored today with a posthumous star on the Hollywood Walk of Fame. Director Guillermo del Toro paid tribute to the Italian artist, describing him as a “worldwide maestro of magic” for his contributions to the film industry.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-15/carlo-rambaldi-honored-with-posthumous-hollywood-walk-of-fam.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Rambaldi, who passed away in 2012 at age 86, is most famous for designing the iconic title character in Steven Spielberg’s 1982 film, “E.T. the Extra-Terrestrial.” During his distinguished career, he earned three Academy Awards for his groundbreaking work in special effects.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately captures the essence of the source text, including the posthumous honor and relevant career details.</p>
