       <h1>Christy Carlson Romano Alleges Pay Disparity on 'Even Stevens'</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#entertainment</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Christy Carlson Romano has claimed she was paid half the salary of co-star Shia LaBeouf during their time on the Disney Channel series 'Even Stevens.' Despite serving as co-leads with equal screen time, Romano alleges a significant pay gap existed between the two actors.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-15/christy-carlson-romano-alleges-pay-disparity-on-even-stevens.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The series, which aired from 2000 to 2003, focused on the comedic relationship between a brother and sister. Romano recently spoke out about her experiences on the production, highlighting the disparity she faced while working on the show.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Concise and accurate summary of the reported claims, maintaining the source's tone and framing.</p>
