     <article class="story single" data-beat="business">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">BUSINESS</span> · Business Standard · 2026-10-15 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Cognizant Leases Over 6.45 Lakh Sq Ft in Chennai for Five Years</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Cognizant</span> <span>#Real Estate</span> <span>#Chennai</span> <span>#Office Lease</span></div>
       <p>Cognizant Technology Solutions India has leased 645,172 square feet of commercial space in Chennai for a five-year term, with a monthly rent of ₹4.77 crore. Transaction documents accessed by Propstack indicate the IT major will pay ₹74 per square foot for this chargeable area. The leased space spans from the ground to the ninth floor of Tower 3 at Embassy Splendid TechZone Block 1, an office park situated in Chennai’s Pallavaram locality. The agreement includes a 15 percent rent escalation every three years.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-15/cognizant-leases-over-645-lakh-sq-ft-in-chennai-for-five-yea.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>This new lease follows other recent real estate activities by Cognizant. In September, the company signed a lease agreement for 141,392 sq ft with flexible workspace operator WeWork India, also located in the Pallavaram-based office park on Pallavaram-Thoraipakkam Road. Additionally, in 2025, Cognizant renewed its office lease at Mindspace Business Parks in Navi Mumbai, securing 92,208 sq ft for five years at a monthly rent of ₹62,70,144.</p><p>The deal reflects a dynamic period in India’s real estate market, which is experiencing record office absorption. A report by Anarock Research &amp; Advisory noted that net absorption reached 49.2 million square feet in the first nine months of 2026, marking a 2 percent year-on-year growth from 48.2 msf in the same period last year. Notably, co-working spaces have surpassed information technology and IT-enabled services as the largest office occupiers for the first time in a nine-month period. Knight Frank India also reported stable office leasing across eight key markets, totaling 66.7 million square feet in the first nine months of 2026, mirroring previous year levels.</p><p>What to watch: Continued expansion by IT firms in key Indian real estate markets.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article provides a precise and well-structured summary of the lease agreement and broader market context using the provided source material.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.business-standard.com/companies/news/cognizant-leases-645-000-sq-ft-in-chennai-at-4-77-crore-monthly-rent-126101501335_1.html" rel="noopener">Business Standard</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       <div class="cityguide"><b>City guide</b><p>More on <a href="https://bharatdn.com/city/chennai/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Chennai</a> - census 2011 population, live weather and air quality, local food and getaways.</p></div>
