     <article class="story single" data-beat="finance">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">FINANCE</span> · Livemint Money · 2026-10-15 · editor 9/10 · 2 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>EPFO Extends September PF Filing to October 31: What It Means for Your Contributions</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#EPFO</span> <span>#PF</span> <span>#Provident Fund</span> <span>#Deadline</span></div>
       <p>The Employees’ Provident Fund Organisation (EPFO) has extended the deadline for employers to file the Electronic Challan-cum-Return (ECR) and deposit statutory provident fund contributions for September 2026. The new deadline is October 31, providing establishments an additional 16 days from the original October 15 cutoff to complete compliance formalities. This extension, announced in a circular dated October 13, 2026, responds to representations from employers facing technical, operational, and administrative difficulties.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-15/epfo-extends-september-pf-filing-to-october-31-what-it-means.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The primary reason for this extension is the recent revision of the statutory PF wage ceiling. Effective September 17, 2026, the mandatory PF coverage wage ceiling was raised from ₹15,000 to ₹25,000 a month. This mid-month change necessitated employers to update their payroll systems, adjust pay bills, and recalculate employee-wise contributions to reflect the new rules. EPFO acknowledged these changes made it challenging for some employers to meet the initial filing and payment deadlines. The extension aims to facilitate accurate and timely filings, though it does not waive statutory obligations for establishments.</p><p>For employees, while employers are responsible for filing the ECR and remitting contributions, it is prudent to check your provident fund records to ensure correct credits. After your employer files the return and contributions are credited, review your PF passbook for September. Verify that the recorded contribution aligns with the applicable PF rules and your eligible wages. If contributions are not reflected, contact your employer's payroll team for clarification. Employees should note that this extension is for employer compliance and does not require them to file separate PF returns.</p><p>The extended deadline specifically applies to the September 2026 wage month's ECR filing and contribution remittance, which must be completed by October 31, 2026, adhering to the Code on Social Security, 2020, and relevant schemes. EPFO has also instructed its field offices to inform local establishments about this extension to assist with compliance. The circular clarifies that this is not a blanket extension for other wage months.</p><p>What to watch: Ensure your September PF contributions are correctly reflected in your passbook by early November.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The report captures all relevant facts from the source, including the specific dates and reasons for the extension.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.livemint.com/money/personal-finance/epfo-extends-september-2026-pf-filing-deadline-to-31-october-what-employees-should-check-11792073749414.html" rel="noopener">Livemint Money</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
