     <article class="story single" data-beat="education">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">EDUCATION</span> · Education (aggregate) · 2026-10-15 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>France Aims to Host 30,000 Indian Students by 2030</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Education</span> <span>#Careers</span></div>
       <p>France has set an ambitious target to welcome 30,000 Indian students to the country by the year 2030. This goal was articulated by French Deputy Ambassador Lisa Amon during the Choose France Tour 2026 event. The announcement was reported by EdexLive.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-15/france-aims-to-host-30000-indian-students-by-2030.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Deputy Ambassador Amon's statement highlights France's commitment to strengthening educational ties with India and attracting a significant number of students for higher education opportunities. The Choose France Tour 2026 serves as a key platform for promoting these initiatives.</p><p>The target of 30,000 Indian students by 2030 underscores a strategic vision for international academic collaboration. This initiative aims to foster greater cultural and educational exchange between the two nations over the coming years.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Effectively captures the core announcement and context from the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://news.google._?oc=5" rel="noopener">Education (aggregate)</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
