     <article class="story single" data-beat="science">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SCIENCE</span> · BBC Science · 2026-10-15 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Hillingdon Council Names and Shames Alleged Fly Tippers on Social Media</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#science</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Hillingdon Council has begun publishing CCTV images of individuals allegedly caught fly tipping on social media and public screens to combat illegal waste dumping. Cabinet member Adam Bennett stated the initiative aims to hold perpetrators accountable, noting that recent posts have garnered over 850,000 views and 2,500 comments from the public.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-15/hillingdon-council-names-and-shames-alleged-fly-tippers-on-s.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The council, which issues £1,000 fixed penalty fines for the offense, views the tactic as a necessary step to deter environmental crime. While some officials are monitoring the effectiveness of this &quot;naming and shaming&quot; approach, the local authority maintains it will continue identifying suspects to protect community spaces from being blighted by waste.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: All concrete facts from the text are present within the brevity limit.</p>
