       <h1>India Secures ₹4,106 Crore Defence Deals for IAF and Navy</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Defence</span> <span>#India</span> <span>#IAF</span> <span>#Navy</span></div>
       <p>India has signed defence deals worth ₹4,106 crore, according to SSBCrack. These significant agreements are aimed at bolstering the capabilities of both the Indian Air Force (IAF) and the Indian Navy.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-15/india-secures-4106-crore-defence-deals-for-iaf-and-navy.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Specifically, the deals include procurement for an IAF satellite and torpedoes for the Navy. These acquisitions highlight ongoing efforts to modernize and enhance India's defence infrastructure across different branches of its armed forces.</p><p>What to watch: Further details on the operational deployment and strategic impact of these new assets.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article is accurate based on the provided summary, though it is thin due to the limited source material provided.</p>
