       <h1>India Welcomes Arrest of Illinois Teen Over Hindu Temple Shooting Plot</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The Consulate General of India in Chicago has commended US law enforcement for arresting 19-year-old Alexandros Paporakis, who allegedly plotted a mass shooting at an Illinois Hindu temple. Police discovered a manifesto containing white supremacist views and references to violence against people of Indian descent, alongside a rifle, tactical gear, and loaded magazines at the suspect's residence. Paporakis now faces charges including making a terrorist threat and unlawful weapon possession.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-15/india-welcomes-arrest-of-illinois-teen-over-hindu-temple-sho.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The investigation began following reports of concerning electronic messages. Police alerted local Hindu places of worship to the threat, and a judge has ordered the suspect to remain in custody pending further legal proceedings.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Concise and accurate summary of the arrest and the nature of the alleged threat.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
