       <h1>Leela Palaces Hotels Shares Surge to Record High Following Strong Q2 Results</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#finance</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Leela Palaces Hotels &amp; Resorts shares climbed 10 percent to a record ₹649.80 after reporting a 27 percent increase in profit after tax to ₹94.6 crore for the second quarter. Operating revenue rose 33 percent year-on-year to ₹411.9 crore, bolstered by a 30 percent increase in Revenue Per Available Room. Growth was driven by strong domestic travel and MICE demand, prompting analysts at Jefferies to raise their EBITDA and PAT estimates.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-15/leela-palaces-hotels-shares-surge-to-record-high-following-s.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The company maintains a pipeline of 10 new properties, with several luxury hotel projects scheduled for opening through 2030. Following the robust performance, analysts have reiterated a 'BUY' rating with a revised price target of ₹735.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurate summary of financial performance, analyst outlook, and development pipeline.</p>
