       <h1>Lisandro Martinez Fined and Issues Apology After Criticizing Manchester United</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#sports</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Manchester United defender Lisandro Martinez has issued an official apology following controversial comments regarding the club's hierarchy. Martinez had publicly criticized the management for providing head coach Michael Carrick with an under-equipped squad after a Champions League loss to Atletico Madrid.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-15/lisandro-martinez-fined-and-issues-apology-after-criticizing.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Following discussions with the club on Thursday, Martinez was formally fined for his outburst. The 28-year-old remains under contract with an option for a one-year extension, as the team prepares for Sunday’s match against Leeds United while currently sitting 13th in the Premier League table.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Captures the Martinez apology, fine, and club context concisely.</p>
