     <article class="story single" data-beat="entertainment">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENTERTAINMENT</span> · Bollywood Hungama · 2026-10-15 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Niti Taylor Recalls Alleged Casting Couch Incident with Telugu Director</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#entertainment</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Actress Niti Taylor has revealed she faced a casting couch incident early in her career involving the director of her 2012 debut Telugu film, 'Mem Vayasuku Vacham.' According to Taylor, the filmmaker requested she sleep with him to secure a role in a subsequent project. She responded by blocking the director and informing her mother.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-15/niti-taylor-recalls-alleged-casting-couch-incident-with-telu.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Shaken by the encounter, Taylor decided to pivot away from films toward a career in television. She went on to gain widespread fame in series like 'Kaisi Yeh Yaariaan,' 'Ghulaam,' and 'Ishqbaaaz,' establishing herself as a prominent face in the Indian television industry.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately reports the details provided in the source text, including the specific film debut and the career pivot.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
