       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · News18 India · 2026-10-15 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Prashant Bhushan Defends Calls for Regime Change</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Advocate Prashant Bhushan stated in Delhi that demanding a change in government is a protected form of democratic expression. He argued that such calls are not unusual, noting that the Bharatiya Janata Party (BJP) previously participated in similar protests while in opposition.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-15/prashant-bhushan-defends-calls-for-regime-change.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Bhushan dismissed allegations that these demands constitute a conspiracy. He questioned why the BJP, having engaged in past demonstrations for regime change, now criticizes others for exercising the same right. He maintained that expressing views on who should govern the country is a fundamental aspect of the democratic process.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately captures the essence of Bhushan's defense and his contextual comparison to BJP's past actions.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.news18.com/india/we-all-want-regime-change-prashant-bhushan-on-agenda-behind-protest-against-sir-cec-10383625.html" rel="noopener">News18 India</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
