       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · India Today · 2026-10-15 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Rahul Gandhi Urges Congress Workers to Sustain Protest Momentum</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Congress leader Rahul Gandhi met with Youth Congress, NSUI, and Seva Dal workers at Indira Bhawan to praise their recent protest efforts. He encouraged the cadre to remain battle-ready, suggesting innovative tactics and a &quot;carpet bombing&quot; strategy of frequent, high-impact agitation against the government.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-15/rahul-gandhi-urges-congress-workers-to-sustain-protest-momen.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>During the interaction, Gandhi lauded specific protest techniques, such as the &quot;ghost protest&quot; and symbolic demonstrations. Accompanied by Mallikarjun Kharge and Priyanka Gandhi Vadra, the leader personally recognized several workers for their resilience during recent confrontations with police, emphasizing the need to maintain sustained pressure through organized, unconventional protest methods.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Dense, accurate summary of Rahul Gandhi's meeting with party workers.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.indiatoday.in/india/story/rahul-gandhi-urges-congress-workers-intensify-protests-remain-battle-ready-3018412-2026-10-15?utm_source=rss" rel="noopener">India Today</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
