     <article class="story single" data-beat="sports">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SPORTS</span> · NDTV Sports · 2026-10-15 · editor 9/10 · 2 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Samson Acknowledges Bumrah's Irreplaceability After India's Loss to West Indies</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Cricket</span> <span>#India</span> <span>#West Indies</span> <span>#Sanju Samson</span></div>
       <p>India wicketkeeper-batter Sanju Samson stated that there is no replacement for a bowler of Jasprit Bumrah's caliber, as India grapples with bowling challenges in the ongoing white-ball series against the West Indies. Bumrah was rested for the T20I series following his participation in the Asian Games, a move by the BCCI to manage the workload of the fast bowler. In his absence, India's bowling attack has been tested on the flat pitches encountered in the series. Samson reiterated in the post-match press conference, &quot;There is no replacement for Jasprit Bumrah. He is a once-in-a-generation kind of bowler, and we are very lucky to have him.&quot;</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-15/samson-acknowledges-bumrahs-irreplaceability-after-indias-lo.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Despite Bumrah's absence, Samson expressed confidence in emerging talent within the squad. He highlighted the performances of Arshdeep Singh, who he noted &quot;has been doing a great job,&quot; and Prince Yadav, whose bowling in recent games was described as &quot;very impressive.&quot; Samson believes that with more opportunities and backing, these young talents will improve. Following the 24-run loss in the fourth T20I at the Rajiv Gandhi International Stadium, Samson also provided an update on Arshdeep Singh, who took a blow to his left arm while batting. Samson stated, &quot;Arshdeep is putting ice on his shoulder,&quot; and expressed hope for his recovery in time for the fifth T20I on Saturday.</p><p>Samson also lauded West Indies captain Shai Hope for his consistent batting performances against India. Hope has scored two centuries and a fifty across the four T20I games, in addition to two centuries in the preceding ODI series. Samson acknowledged Hope's approach, noting he plays &quot;really good cricketing shots, not taking that much risk,&quot; and respects the bowlers. &quot;We need to give the credit to him for the way he is batting, and we are definitely switched on how to respond to him every game,&quot; Samson added.</p><p>The wicketkeeper-batter further backed India’s top order, specifically Ishan Kishan and Abhishek Sharma, despite Sharma's struggle in the fourth match where he made 29 from 24 balls. Samson called them &quot;the world's best top two batters,&quot; emphasizing that &quot;one game is okay.&quot; He pointed out Abhishek’s &quot;really good 70 (69)&quot; in the previous game and Ishan's consistent scoring. Samson identified Tilak Varma's dismissal in the 17th over as the turning point of the match, stating India was &quot;cruising, scoring those 10-12 runs per over really nicely&quot; when Varma and Nitish Reddy were batting together. He praised Reddy and Varma for their composure under pressure after losing five wickets.</p><p>What to watch: India's bowling strategy in the decisive upcoming matches against the West Indies.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately reflects the source material and Sanju Samson's comments regarding the team's performance and individual players.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://sports.ndtv.com/cricket/no-replacement-for-jasprit-bumrah-but-weve-talent-coming-along-sanju-samson-after-hyderabad-loss-12188403#publisher=newsstand" rel="noopener">NDTV Sports</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
